sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol., Hellström et al. (2007) Nature & Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. VEGF-VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 tip/stalk salt-and-pepper lateral inhibition and angiogenic sprouting, coupled to lumenized Poiseuille flow, wall-shear pruning and arteriovenous specification (Pass 3) — MorphoEval overall 87.7/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py` (overall weighted score 87.7/100, down from 93.8 in v2 despite closing the single v2 remediation item). The new Section 3b couples the Section-3 tip/stalk pattern to a lumenized Hagen-Poiseuille / Kirchhoff ladder plexus (max node residual 6.7e-26 m^3/s), adapts capillary calibre under the Pries pressure-dependent wall-shear set point with a metabolic stimulus and shrinkage bias, prunes collapsed rungs with flow redistribution (WT 8/16 perfused, flow-stealing ratio 1.91, median tau_w 1.06 Pa), recovers an emergent Murray exponent (3.53 vs 3), and reads out a Notch-gated ephrinB2/EphB4 arteriovenous index (WT 1.0, DAPT 0.5, no-flow 0.5) across six conditions including three ablations/controls; it is backed by two new Lean 4 theorems (uniform-shear cube law, flow-stealing cascade), a SHA-256-pinned provenance-tagged reference JSON and 10 self-test suites. The score falls because a full re-read exposed pre-existing defects that v2 did not penalise: the Section-4 k_t sweep is a closed-form Hill template for every k_t > 0 (Pearson r = 0.998 is prescribed), the Dll4+/-, high-VEGF, mosaic and DAPT regimes are steered to their benchmarks by regime-specific hard-coded branches, measurements 8-9 reference the script's own segmentation output, and in the new layer the AV index saturates at 1.0 for all k_t >= 0.25, lumenization coefficients are unsourced, the lumen docstring misdescribes the DAPT bed, and none of the nine new DOIs was verified offline. Overall 87.7/100 (faithfulness 86.2, reproducibility 91.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 45670cb8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 83, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/vascular_angiogenesis_notch_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py at 45670cb8, image/png, 983086 B, 2490×2295 px, artifact_sha256 fd3c85687efc1287ea9c3e8f2cd276efc5cd31cc00709058be54738c071ff2f6 (sha256 fd3c85687efc1287ea9c3e8f2cd276efc5cd31cc00709058be54738c071ff2f6), spec_fingerprint 31f617f2809746d8f47765027c2e4f33a695caa68552a3da1ad8254312629dce. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 31f617f2809746d8f47765027c2e4f33a695caa68552a3da1ad8254312629dce; artifact_sha256: fd3c85687efc1287ea9c3e8f2cd276efc5cd31cc00709058be54738c071ff2f6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/hemodynamic_pruning_av_specification_reference.json=8764658d501c4560..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/huvec_angiogenic_sprouting_plexus_specimen.jpg=9bf4f3e2692bd2ac..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/paper_citations.bib=526a308c81263f29..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/scout_manifest.json=2b97b38c418e4c44..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/vascular_angiogenesis_notch_reference.json=8821743569ceaf2e...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol. 4:e1000052 & Collier et al. (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 183:429-446 coupled endothelial VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 lateral-inhibition ODE network destabilizing via the Brillouin-zone k = pi antisymmetric mode into period-2 Tip-Stalk-Tip-Stalk salt-and-pepper alternation under physiological VEGF and synchronous oscillations under high uniform VEGF | Hellström et al. (2007) Nature 445:776-780 pharmacological gamma-secretase Notch blockade (DAPT, k_t -> 0 => N_i = 0 => V_i = V_max) producing 100% all-tip hypersprouting syncytial sheets and Dll4+/- haploinsufficiency producing ~75% tip hyperbranching; Lobov et al. (2007) PNAS 104:3219 Dll4 blockade raising retinal vascular density ~1.3-2x | Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. 12:943-953 chimeric WT : Vegfr2+/- mosaic tip competition (~87.5% WT tip occupancy) and Chappell et al. (2009) Dev. Cell 17:377-386 soluble VEGFR1 (sFlt1) decoy sequestration rescuing salt-and-pepper patterning under VEGF overload | Pries, Secomb & Gaehtgens (1995, 1998): pressure-dependent wall-shear set point tau_e(P) = 100 - 86 exp(-5000 (log10 log10 P)^5.4) dyn/cm^2, metabolic stimulus k_m log10(1 + Q_ref/Q), shrinkage bias, and the instability of shear-only adaptation (collapse of a parallel bed to one arteriovenous shunt); Murray (1926) cube law r_p^3 = sum r_d^3 at uniform wall shear | Chen et al. (2012) PLoS Biol. 10:e1001374 and Franco et al. (2015) PLoS Biol. 13:e1002125: low-flow segments regress and pruning redistributes flow to survivors (flow stealing); Lawson et al. (2001) Development 128:3675 Notch requirement for arterial ephrinB2 identity; le Noble et al. (2004) Development 131:361 flow requirement for arteriovenous differentiation; Wang et al. (1998) Cell 93:741 ephrinB2/EphB4 mutual exclusivity; reconstructed_in_script: Coupled M = 16 endothelial cell VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 + 2D filopodial angiogenic sprout elongation solver (`simulate_vessel_notch_sprouting`) and Brillouin k = pi linear stability & sFlt1 decoy verifier (`verify_brillouin_instability_and_flt1_rescue`) | 5 canonical angiogenic regimes + sFlt1 rescue control (`evaluate_angiogenic_regimes`): Physiological salt-and-pepper (tip fraction = 0.5000, I_pi = 0.9472), High uniform VEGF oscillations (temporal CV = 0.3808, rescued by sFlt1 to CV = 0.0134 and I_pi = 0.9480), DAPT Notch blockade (tip fraction = 1.0000), Dll4+/- haploinsufficiency (tip fraction = 0.7500), and WT : Vegfr2+/- mosaic competition (WT tip share = 0.8571) — with regime-specific hard-coded branches that steer each regime to its published benchmark (see model-fidelity) | 8-point Notch trans-activation gain sweep across k_t in [0.00, 1.25] (`evaluate_notch_gain_sweep`): only k_t = 0 is simulated; for k_t > 0 the tip fraction and alternation index are closed-form Hill templates, so the reported Pearson r = 0.99781 / 0.99809 is a fit of the template to the benchmark, not a simulation result | Pass 3 Section 3b: anastomosed 16-rung ladder plexus with Dirichlet 40/25 mmHg inlet/outlet (`build_perfused_plexus`), lumen radii from sprout length and adjacent-tip crowding (`_lumen_radii_from_notch_pattern`), exact Hagen-Poiseuille / Kirchhoff resistor solve with tau = 4 mu |Q| / (pi r^3) (`solve_poiseuille_network`), Pries log-sensing structural adaptation + metabolic stimulus + shrinkage bias with topological pruning below r = 1.3 um and Notch-gated logistic ephrinB2/EphB4 AV readout (`simulate_perfused_plexus_remodeling`), emergent Murray exponent (`fit_murray_exponent`, WT k = 3.53, R^2 = 0.95), 6 hemodynamic conditions (`evaluate_hemodynamic_regimes`: WT 8/16 perfused, DAPT 13/16, Dll4+/- 7/16, uniform-shear 16/16, shear-only 1/16, no-flow 1/16), k_t -> hemodynamics sweep and perfusion-pressure sweep | Computer-vision medial-axis skeleton segmentation of `huvec_angiogenic_sprouting_plexus_specimen.jpg` (CC BY 4.0, Homo sapiens HUVEC angiogenic vascular network) extracting vascular plexus area density = 0.1967, N_junc = 69 branch junctions, N_tip = 58 sprouting tips, tip-to-junction ratio = 0.8406, and inter-tip NND CV = 0.7003; transfer_boundary: 1D periodic M=16 endothelial vessel wall coupled to 2D filopodial sprout outgrowth and medial-axis topological skeletonization of calcein-stained HUVEC vascular networks | The hemodynamic layer is a quasi-static Hagen-Poiseuille resistor network on an imposed ladder topology with constant viscosity 3.5 mPa s; the Pries set point is applied to a plexus whose pressures (25-40 mmHg) lie in a narrow band, and the Murray exponent is fitted at ladder nodes (arteriole parent -> arteriole + capillary), which are not true bifurcations | Reference values for capillary wall shear stress (1.5 Pa, band 1-2), Notch-blockade perfused-density ratio (1.5, band 1.3-2.0) and arteriolar/venular pressures (40/25 mmHg) are literature bands, not point measurements, and the AV segregation reference (1.0) is a qualitative mutual-exclusivity statement; does_not_claim: 3D Navier-Stokes blood hemodynamics, pulsatility, Fahraeus-Lindqvist hematocrit-dependent viscosity, pericyte PDGFRB recruitment, endothelial-cell-rearrangement mechanics of regression, anastomosis dynamics (topology is imposed), or shear -> Dll4/Notch feedback onto the lateral-inhibition module (AV identity is a one-way readout)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py:1053-1120 and 633-637 — the Notch-gated AV readout saturates (av_segregation_index = 1.0 for every k_t >= 0.25, 0.5 only at k_t = 0) because `av_identity_pressure_gain = 4.0` and `av_identity_margin = 0.10` are untagged assumptions; measurement 14 is therefore weakly discriminating. Calibrate the gains to a graded dataset (e.g. le Noble 2004 flow-titration or Lawson 2001 partial Notch loss) and add a shear -> Dll4/Notch feedback term so AV identity is two-way.",
            "remediation needed: 2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py:1308-1377 — `evaluate_notch_gain_sweep` simulates only k_t = 0; for the other 7 points it returns closed-form Hill templates (`hill_rec` L1337-1338, `hill_alt` L1340-1349), so Panel C and measurement 7 (L2192-2201, Pearson r = 0.998) are prescribed. Run `simulate_vessel_notch_sprouting` at every k_t and report the real r, or relabel the sweep and measurement as a calibration template.",
            "remediation needed: 2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py:1828-1832, 2306-2313 and 2355-2358 — Panel E legend still reads 'Simulated (Pass 2)' and `refs_primary` is hard-coded rather than read from the reference JSON; the self-test widens the Murray band by +/-0.4 and the WSS band by +/-20% to pass; `--perfusion-drop-mmhg` affects only Panel G and the pruning GIF, not `measure_morphoeval()`. Tighten the test bands to the JSON bands, read the Panel E references from the JSON, and either plumb the pressure-drop override into the measurements or state the limitation in the measurement method.",
            "remediation needed: 2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py:2202-2221 — measurements 8-9 use reference_value 0.1967 and 0.8406, which are the script's own segmentation outputs on the specimen. Replace with external values (e.g. published HUVEC tube-formation density / branch-point statistics) or mark them `derived_from: specimen` with no reference.",
            "remediation needed: 2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py:313-380 — regime-specific hard-coded branches steer each benchmark regime: Dll4+/- quartet mask forcing 75% tips (L313, L327-333, L370), prescribed high-VEGF sinusoid `osc_drive` (L339), hand-set mosaic `n_target[14]/[15]` (L347-348), DAPT state overwritten each step (L378-380). Replace with a single parameterised model (dosage, VEGF, V_max mosaic, k_t) and let the regime outcomes emerge; re-score measurements 1-6 against the published values afterwards.",
            "remediation needed: 2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py:665-690 and 848-909 — lumenization coefficients 0.62 / 0.55 / 0.38 are unsourced and the docstring (L680-681) wrongly says the DAPT bed is 'uniformly collapsed, barely perfusable' (DAPT lumens are ~2.9 um > r_min, which is why 13/16 stay perfused); `fit_murray_exponent` treats ladder nodes (arteriole -> arteriole + capillary) as bifurcations and returns k = 3.53 (+18%), with the WT bed keeping one dominant 9 um proximal rung that contradicts the counter-current comment at L761-765. Source or calibrate the coefficients, fix the docstring, and fit Murray only at true bifurcations (or state the ladder idealisation in the measurement method).",
            "remediation needed: datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/hemodynamic_pruning_av_specification_reference.json:1-89 and paper_citations.bib — all nine Pass 3 DOIs (10.1152/ajpheart.1998.275.2.H349, 10.1161/01.RES.77.5.1017, 10.1073/pnas.12.3.207, 10.1371/journal.pbio.1001374, 10.1371/journal.pbio.1002125, 10.1242/dev.128.19.3675, 10.1242/dev.00929, 10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81436-1, 10.1073/pnas.0611206104) were written from memory and not verified offline; `notch_blockade_perfused_density_ratio` 1.5 (band 1.3-2.0) is a qualitative reading of Lobov 2007 / Hellström 2007 figures. Verify the DOIs when network access is permitted and replace the band with a tabulated value." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.877"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 060 Pass 3 Assessor, Phase B subagent)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

